```
Hierarchical tags: add/deny/mixed/remove a tag on the selected metarecord(s), or list the vocabulary. Encapsulates the subsumption and exclusivity rules (drop ancestors on add, descendants on deny, and whatever the new answer contradicts). The field-name convention is configurable via the `[tag]` config table

Usage: mf tag [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     The record(s) have the tag (drops more general ancestor tags, and the negatives on the tag or its ancestors)
  deny    The record(s) do NOT have the tag (drops more specific descendant negatives, and the positives on the tag or its descendants)
  mixed   Mark the folder(s) mixed w.r.t. the tag
  remove  Drop the tag from the record(s) (undo of add)
  list    List the tag vocabulary as TSV: path<TAB>partition<TAB>exclusive
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -q, --query <QUERY>
          DSL query selector (use -s for the simplified language)

  -i, --id <ID>
          Single-metarecord selector by UUID

      --eq <EQ>
          Exact-match selector: name[:type]=value (repeatable, AND-ed)

  -s, --simplified
          Treat -q as simplified-language text and expand it first

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
